---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="SkanPay - QR Checkout Gateway"
  description="SkanPay helps merchants and payment partners coordinate QR checkout requests, customer approval, coupon or voucher logic, and merchant-readable results."
  activePath="/"
>
  <section class="product-hero">
    <div class="product-hero-copy">
      <div class="brand-kicker">
        <img src="/skanpay-logo.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
        <span>SkanPay QR Payment Gateway</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Turn a QR scan into a checkout result the store can trust.</h1>
      <p class="lead-copy">
        SkanPay is building patent-pending QR payment gateway technology for in-store checkout, customer approval, coupon or voucher logic, and partner handoff.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Start a Conversation</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/qr-payments/">View Technology</a>
      </div>
      <dl class="hero-facts" aria-label="SkanPay focus">
        <div>
          <dt>Audience</dt>
          <dd>Merchants, banks, wallets, loyalty and payment partners</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Stage</dt>
          <dd>Patent-pending gateway invention with BeamCash demo available</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <aside class="checkout-brief" aria-label="SkanPay checkout packet example">
      <div class="brief-header">
        <span>Checkout packet</span>
        <strong>Store counter / QR request</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="brief-lines">
        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Merchant creates request with amount and session reference.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Customer scans and reviews merchant, amount, and checkout context.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Payment, wallet, coupon, or voucher logic returns a decision.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Store receives a readable result: confirmed, redeemed, cancelled, or expired.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="brief-result">
        <span>Merchant result</span>
        <strong>Clear enough for staff to close or retry the sale.</strong>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section business-section">
    <div class="business-heading">
      <span>Why SkanPay</span>
      <h2>QR payment needs more than a code on a counter.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="comparison-table" aria-label="QR checkout before and with SkanPay">
      <div class="comparison-row heading">
        <span>Common QR setup</span>
        <span>SkanPay approach</span>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-row">
        <p>Static QR code leaves staff asking whether a customer actually completed the action.</p>
        <p>Each checkout request has a state the merchant can read.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-row">
        <p>Coupon or voucher redemption becomes a separate manual process.</p>
        <p>Offer logic can be coordinated inside the checkout handoff.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-row">
        <p>Wallet, payment, loyalty, and merchant systems blur responsibilities.</p>
        <p>Partners can discuss a defined request, decision, and result boundary.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section fit-section">
    <div class="business-heading narrow">
      <span>Where it fits</span>
      <h2>Built for checkout conversations with merchants and partners.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="fit-columns">
      <div>
        <span>Merchant</span>
        <h3>Store-facing confirmation</h3>
        <p>Staff need to see whether a request is open, pending, confirmed, redeemed, cancelled, or expired.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>Customer</span>
        <h3>Approval with context</h3>
        <p>The customer should know who they are paying, what they are approving, and what value is applied.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>Partner</span>
        <h3>Defined handoff</h3>
        <p>Banks, wallets, loyalty apps, and payment partners can evaluate their role before integration work begins.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section demo-feature">
    <div>
      <div class="demo-feature-label">
        <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-logo.svg" alt="BeamCash" />
      </div>
      <h2>BeamCash is the working demo under SkanPay.</h2>
      <p>
        BeamCash gives partners something tangible to review: a seller QR surface, a customer checkout screen, and a simple approval flow.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/beamcash-demo/">Review the BeamCash demo</a>
    </div>
    <div class="screen-pair" aria-label="BeamCash demo screens">
      <figure>
        <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-seller-dashboard-mobile.png" alt="BeamCash seller dashboard with QR code" />
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-buyer-checkout-mobile.png" alt="BeamCash buyer checkout screen" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section stage-section">
    <div>
      <span>Current stage</span>
      <h2>Patent-pending gateway work, ready for serious review.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="stage-list">
      <div>
        <strong>Technology</strong>
        <p>QR checkout coordination, coupon or voucher redemption paths, app handoff, and merchant-readable results.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Demo</strong>
        <p>BeamCash is used to show seller setup, QR display, customer scan, and checkout approval.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Next conversations</strong>
        <p>Merchant pilots, wallet participation, bank or processor fit, and loyalty or offer program use cases.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="business-cta">
    <div>
      <span>Contact</span>
      <h2>Discuss a merchant, wallet, bank, or partner use case.</h2>
    </div>
    <a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Contact SkanPay</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
